WEBVTT

00:00:08,750 --> 00:00:13,750
Do you have a protocol for fibromyalgia?

00:00:13,750 --> 00:00:17,750
No, no.

00:00:17,750 --> 00:00:19,750
So, the reason why it all,

00:00:19,750 --> 00:00:23,750
because there's reasons why a person would have the symptoms of fibromyalgia.

00:00:23,750 --> 00:00:26,750
fibromyalgia is not a disease in itself.

00:00:26,750 --> 00:00:29,750
fibromyalgia is a collection of symptoms.

00:00:29,750 --> 00:00:30,750
It's a syndrome.

00:00:30,750 --> 00:00:35,750
So, you have to figure out why a person has this collection of symptoms.

00:00:35,750 --> 00:00:37,750
Do they have an autoimmune issue?

00:00:37,750 --> 00:00:39,750
So, they have antibodies to self-tissue.

00:00:39,750 --> 00:00:40,750
Very common.

00:00:40,750 --> 00:00:42,750
They have antibodies to collagen.

00:00:42,750 --> 00:00:44,750
They have antibodies to their,

00:00:44,750 --> 00:00:48,750
to their, you know, upper motor neuron, brain issue.

00:00:48,750 --> 00:00:53,750
So, running labs that will look for antibodies to self-tissue

00:00:53,750 --> 00:00:55,750
would be in order.

00:00:55,750 --> 00:01:01,750
Also, with fibromyalgia, you could have some sort of chronic infection.

00:01:01,750 --> 00:01:06,750
The chronic Lyme type issue can be an issue with fibromyalgia.

00:01:06,750 --> 00:01:08,750
So, you don't want to,

00:01:08,750 --> 00:01:10,750
and I'd recommend this with,

00:01:10,750 --> 00:01:12,750
but just about everything,

00:01:12,750 --> 00:01:15,750
there's, you don't want to go to somebody who's just going to,

00:01:15,750 --> 00:01:18,750
here's my, here's my fibromyalgia protocol.

00:01:18,750 --> 00:01:22,750
Or, here's this protocol for this disease.

00:01:22,750 --> 00:01:25,750
I'm not saying somebody might not be helped by that,

00:01:25,750 --> 00:01:29,750
but, you know, you have to get to the reason why.

00:01:29,750 --> 00:01:31,750
You're just going to dig to the reason why,

00:01:31,750 --> 00:01:33,750
and try to figure that out,

00:01:33,750 --> 00:01:35,750
and then treat the reason why.

00:01:35,750 --> 00:01:38,750
You've got treating the name disorder,

00:01:38,750 --> 00:01:42,750
or name syndrome, or name disease.

00:01:42,750 --> 00:01:45,750
Unfortunately, that's, that is really what is,

00:01:45,750 --> 00:01:47,750
it's happening in the practice of medicine.

00:01:47,750 --> 00:01:50,750
No, I mean, everybody's just a disease.

00:01:50,750 --> 00:01:54,750
So, the idea of medicine is we come to the name of the disease,

00:01:54,750 --> 00:01:56,750
and then we look up at Merck manual,

00:01:56,750 --> 00:01:59,750
and we give this drug for that disease.

00:01:59,750 --> 00:02:02,750
Well, is it treating the reason why the disease is there?

00:02:02,750 --> 00:02:06,750
No, it's not typically treating why the disease is there.

00:02:06,750 --> 00:02:08,750
It's not addressing the reason why.

00:02:08,750 --> 00:02:10,750
Well, are you helping the patient?

00:02:10,750 --> 00:02:14,750
Well, the drug may effectively decrease that person's symptoms,

00:02:14,750 --> 00:02:17,750
but just because you've decreased the person's symptoms,

00:02:17,750 --> 00:02:22,750
doesn't mean that you've effectively helped that person

00:02:22,750 --> 00:02:28,750
with overall morbidity and issues with mortality for that disease.

00:02:28,750 --> 00:02:31,750
I don't know, I think it's best to look and try to dig in

00:02:31,750 --> 00:02:33,750
to figure out the reason why.

